.TH PCLOUDD 1 "2026-04-15" "pcloud-rs Rust" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
pcloudd \- pCloud background daemon for the Rust rewrite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcloudd
.br
.B pcloudd serve
.br
.B pcloudd --help
.br
.B pcloudd --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pcloudd
is the background service used by
.BR pcloudc (1).
It bootstraps the Rust runtime, owns the local state store, local IPC socket,
auth/session lifecycle, sync engine, transfer runtime, crypto runtime, and
mount runtime.

With no subcommand,
.B pcloudd
prints a one-shot runtime summary and exits.
With
.BR serve ,
it binds the configured local IPC socket and serves requests until shutdown.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B (no subcommand)
Print the current runtime summary and exit.
.TP
.B serve
Run the daemon request loop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Show daemon version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
Override the daemon state root.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_ENV
Select bootstrap environment semantics.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_API_MODE
Select development, plaintext, or TLS API mode.
.SH RUNTIME NOTES
The current daemon binary documents only its real runtime modes. It does not
advertise packaging-only flags that are not implemented by the binary itself.

In secure-default bootstrap, the daemon creates and uses owner-only runtime
paths, including the local IPC socket.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pcloud/
Default development root used by the current bootstrap path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcloudc (1)
